==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sorceress Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Enchantress Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Witch Cat is one of the better non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] options for stalling Red enemies—especially in {{4c}} stages, where many of your usual anti-Red CC options aren't available. Stack enough Witch Cats and short-ranged Reds like [[Bore]] and [[Red Cyclone]] will barely be able to move at all. Even late in the game, she can stall a Bore while others take care of the enemies behind.

However, Witch Cat suffers from Single Attack, making her situationally useful at best even in the early game.

==='''True Form'''===
More range and higher slow duration says it all. With this True Form unlocked, Enchantress Cat can now outrange [[J.K. Bun Bun]], and with a higher slow uptime, she can be more consistent at keeping Red enemies slowed, halting their progress even more.

==='''Talents'''===
Talents allow Enchantress Cat to slow down [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] as well as Red. In this regard she faces competition from Corrupted Psychocat, who has the same talent but works better due to having higher range (360). Still, her 250 range is sufficient to outrange various melee zombie threats, making her a very worthwhile choice against them. Enchantress Cat also has the Survive talent, which makes her even more cost-effective. Making her already long slow duration last even longer is naturally great too. As a CC unit, her Attack and HP Buff Talents are not worth investing in.

==='''Orb'''===
Use a Defense Up for Red if you see yourself using her often. Otherwise leave it empty.

