==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Witch Cat's slow chance from 10% to 20%.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Witch Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Witch Please (Removed Combo)|Witch Please]] and [[Medium Cool (Removed Combo)|Medium Cool]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Witch Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Witch Cat
A Magical Cat that would rather be
a Magical Girl than a Witch.
Might slow Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Sorceress Cat
Obtained magic skills from online courses.
Really popular at parties but doesn't get paid.
Might slow Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Enchantress Cat
Used her clairvoyant powers to scry the
best way to make it big on TV. Her star
power might slow Red enemy movement.</pre>
*The line, "A Cat well into their apprenticeship as a witch, though they'd much rather be a Magical Girl" in Witch Cat's description is likely a reference to ''[[Puella Magi Madoka Magica Collaboration Event|Puella Magi Madoka Magica]]''.
*Sorceress Cat's hat appears to be based on the [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Mad_cap Mad cap], an eye-patterned witch hat in some of the ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest|Dragon Quest]]'' games.
*The line, "A witch whose style of fortune-telling became well known and entered the show business," in Enchantress Cat's Japanese description may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Kazuko Hosoki|Kazuko Hosoki]], a famous fortune teller and TV personality.
*Enchantress Cat's hairstyle resembles that of [[wikia:berserk:Schierke|Schierke]], a witch-in-training from the manga ''[[wikipedia:Berserk (manga)|Berserk]]''.
*Unlike most other units, Witch Cat's color scheme hasn't stayed consistent across spin-offs. In [[Nyanko Defence Force]] she had a black hat and brown hair, but in [[Battle Cats Quest]] it was changed to a purple hat and blonde hair. Another Cat sharing this inconsistency is [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]], being primarily yellow in Nyanko Defence Force rather than blue as it is in The Battle Cats.
**Her Battle Cats Quest design may be a reference to the original design of [https://en.touhouwiki.net/wiki/Marisa_Kirisame Marisa Kirisame] from [[wikipedia:Touhou Project|Touhou Project]], who had a purple hat and blonde hair during Touhou 2 through 5.

